# Vercel Web Analytics Implementation

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this static HTML website following the latest official Vercel documentation.

## What Was Done

### 1. Documentation Research
- Fetched the latest installation instructions from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart
- Identified that this is a static HTML/vanilla JavaScript project with no build framework
- Determined the appropriate integration method for static sites

### 2. Analytics Script Installation
Added the Vercel Web Analytics script to all 12 HTML pages in the project:
- `/index.html` (main homepage)
- `/about/index.html`
- `/contact/index.html`
- `/privacy/index.html`
- `/webcam-test/index.html`
- `/microphone-test/index.html`
- `/speaker-test/index.html`
- `/keyboard-test/index.html`
- `/screen-test/index.html`
- `/touchscreen-test/index.html`
- `/cps-test/index.html`
- `/gamepad-test/index.html`

### 3. Implementation Details
According to Vercel's official documentation for static HTML sites, the analytics script was added to the `<head>` section of each HTML file, just before the closing `</head>` tag:

```html
<!-- Vercel Web Analytics -->
<script>
  window.va = window.va || function () { (window.vaq = window.vaq || []).push(arguments); };
</script>
<script defer src="/_vercel/insights/script.js"></script>
```

This implementation:
- Uses the official Vercel Analytics path `/_vercel/insights/script.js` which is automatically provided by Vercel's platform
- Initializes the `window.va` global function for collecting analytics events
- Uses the `defer` attribute for optimal page load performance
- Works entirely client-side with no build process required

### 4. Package Verification
- Confirmed `@vercel/analytics` package is present in `package.json` (version ^2.0.1)
- Ran `npm install` to ensure all dependencies are properly installed
- No build errors or issues detected

## Technical Approach
Since this is a pure static HTML website (no React, Next.js, Vue, etc.), I followed Vercel's documentation for vanilla JavaScript/static site integration. The script is injected via the CDN path `/_vercel/insights/script.js` which Vercel automatically serves when the site is deployed on their platform.

## Testing Recommendations
Once deployed to Vercel:
1. Navigate to your Vercel dashboard → Your Project → Analytics
2. Enable Web Analytics if not already enabled
3. Visit the deployed site and navigate between pages
4. Verify page views appear in the Analytics dashboard within a few minutes

## Preservation of Existing Code
- All existing HTML structure, styles, and scripts remain unchanged
- Google Analytics (gtag.js) integration remains intact
- No modifications to JavaScript functionality or page layouts
- Analytics script added in a non-intrusive manner that doesn't affect page rendering
